<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Beorhtric of Wessex</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 802</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Beorhtric was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wessex">Wessex</a> from 786 to 802. He married Eadburh, a daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/offa-of-mercia">Offa of Mercia</a>, in 789 and ruled as Offa's ally, while his rival Ecgberht was driven into exile among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-saxon-chronicle">Anglo-Saxon Chronicle</a> records the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> raid on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, at Portland, in his reign. On his death Ecgberht became king, and Beorhtric was buried at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wareham">Wareham</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/beorhtric-of-wessex.jpg" alt="Beorhtric of Wessex" width="320" height="319" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Beorhtric_of_Wessex.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
